```verilog
module TopModule (
    input  [255:0] in,
    input  [7:0]   sel,
    output         out
);

    assign out = in[sel];

endmodule
```

This implements the 256-to-1 multiplexer by directly indexing the packed 256-bit vector `in` with the 8-bit select signal `sel`, so `sel=0` selects `in[0]`, `sel=1` selects `in[1]`, and so on up to `sel=255` selecting `in[255]`.
